Adjust oven rack to lower-middle position and preheat oven to 275°F (135°C).

Pat @beef stew meat{2%lbs} dry with paper towels and sprinkle all over with @kosher salt{} and @ground black pepper{}.

In a large #Dutch oven{}, heat @extra-virgin olive oil{2%tbsp} over high heat until shimmering. Cook half of the beef until browned on all sides, about ~{4-5%minutes}, adjusting heat as necessary to avoid burning. Transfer browned beef to a plate and repeat with remaining beef.

Reduce heat to medium. Add @yellow onion{1}(finely chopped) and @garlic{3%cloves} and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened and lightly browned, about ~{7%minutes}.

Add @piquillo peppers{1}(drained), @carrot{1}(peeled and cut into large chunks), @button mushrooms{8%oz}(quartered if large), @smoked Spanish paprika{1.5%tsp}, @dry red wine{1%cup}, @diced tomatoes{1%28oz can}, @tomato paste{2.5%tbsp}, @Worcestershire sauce{1%tbsp}, @bay leaves{2}, and @thyme{4%sprigs}. Bring to a simmer over medium-high heat. Add beef and juices from the plate to the pot. Cover and transfer to the oven. Cook until beef is tender, about ~{4%hours}.

Remove stew from oven and discard thyme and bay leaves. Reduce over medium-low heat until sauce is thick enough to coat the back of a spoon, about ~{5%minutes}. Season to taste with @kosher salt{} and @ground black pepper{}.

Let cool slightly. Serve with @sour cream{1%cup} or plain yogurt (or 1 cup plain yogurt).
